hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"321","It is narrated by Yusuf bin Musa, it is narrated by Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed God has angels who succeed one another among you. When it was the dawn prayer, the angels of the day descended and witnessed the prayer with you all, then the angels ascended. night, and the angels of the day stayed with you, and their Lord asks them, and He knows best about them: What did you let My servants do? He said: Then they say: We came while they were praying and we left them praying. When it was the afternoon prayer, the angels of the night descended and witnessed the prayer with you all, then they ascended. The angels of the day, and the angels of the night stayed with you. He said: Then their Lord will ask them, and He knows best about them, and He will say: What have you forsaken My servants? What do they do? He said: Then they say: We came while they were praying, and we left them while they were praying. He said: So I thought that they would say: So forgive them that day. ""religion"""
"322","It was narrated by Yahya bin Hakim, it was narrated by Yahya bin Hammad, it was narrated by Abu Awanah, on the authority of Suleiman, and he is Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The angels of the night and the angels of the day gather for the dawn prayer and the afternoon prayer, and they gather In the dawn prayer, the angels of the night ascend, and the angels of the day stand firm, and they gather for the afternoon prayer, so the angels of the day ascend, and they stand firm. Angels of the night, and their Lord asks them: How did you abandon My servants? They say: We came to them while they were praying and left them while they were praying, so forgive me. theirs on the Day of Judgment.”"
